 "problems": [
  "Three dossiers (aboriginal-australians, aboriginal-tasmanians, kuk-swamp-agriculture) stop at the -3400 horizon with confidence-1 dissolve events although the cultures continue; extend them or hand the land to the colonial group, otherwise Australia, Tasmania and the New Guinea highlands go blank from 3399 BCE.",
  "naqada-culture (me-03/xx-01-a) draws Upper Egypt intersect the Nile with 40 km, and early-dynastic-period-of-egypt's Cliopatria shape, over the Egyptian side of Lower Nubia south of the First Cataract (54 and 10 cells of the gazetteer's Lower Nubia); a-group-culture was trimmed by those cells, so the Egyptian group should stop both at Aswan and the A-Group can regain them. The same Nile line also carries 14 cells along the Lake Nasser arms into the Nabta Playa disc, trimmed in nabta-playa-neolithic.",
  "green-sahara-cultures draws the Sahara region (27,973 cells) less Egypt, the Capsian country and the Gobero disc at confidence 1 from the African humid period page; drop it if the project does not want a whole-desert culture on that evidence.",
  "The gazetteer region 'Sahara' contains the Nile valley and the Delta (it covers 722 of 808 cells of maadi-culture and all of naqada-culture's keyframes), which is why Egypt is subtracted wholesale in green-sahara-cultures.",
  "WebFetch returns a model's summary of the page: quotation marks in notes are the quotes as the summary returned them; two page summaries were internally inconsistent (Shaheinab, Gobero) and the inconsistency is stated in the notes.",
  "Cell counts quoted in notes were computed with the gazetteer; four were first written from memory and corrected before the dossiers were finished (watson-brake-culture, oshara-tradition, cochise-culture, old-copper-complex)."
 ],
 "fixes_applied": 0
